## Details

[The XML parser trims the value before schema conversion](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/aee8fe202a2fbd79a7a33cae70b310edc5960aa5/rust/src/parser/src/tool/glm_xml/mod.rs#L254-L270). Removing that trim lets the [existing conversion preserve strings and normalize typed values](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/aee8fe202a2fbd79a7a33cae70b310edc5960aa5/rust/src/parser/src/tool/parameters.rs#L357-L385).

Scope is the Rust frontend's GLM parsers. Targeted live issue/PR searches found no implementing duplicate. [#47179](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/47179) discusses Rust/Python parsing differences generally, and [#48753](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/48753) reports meaningful-whitespace loss in a different Qwen parser; neither supplies this GLM fix. #42026 addressed the separate Python implementation.

